# The drive's command feedforward from LinuxCNC's position stream
# (vel_int0.mode 1) with the unbiased velocity observer (vel1.bc 1), on the
# ironless linear axis (examples/linear_axis.conf): a LinuxCNC-style move at
# 2 m/s^2 (lcnc ... ACC: constant acceleration, vel_cmd the average over
# each period, as joint.N.vel-cmd). vel_int recovers the acceleration
# exactly (2000 mm/s^2 = 209.4 rad/s^2 at 60 mm per revolution) and the
# position error while accelerating is ~0.5 mrad. The stock settings
# (mode 0, bc 0) hold ~3.7 mrad here; either alone does not help (the
# observer's lag under acceleration, 2 d a / w, had been standing in for the
# missing acceleration feedforward).
@args --drive examples/linear_axis.conf --sim examples/linear_axis_sim.txt
debug_level 0
conf0.pos_bw = 60
conf0.vel_bw = 400
vel_int0.mode = 1
vel1.bc = 1
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 0 0 2000
run 0.05
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.01 0.15
vel_int0.acc_out
lcnc 1 0
run 0.3
pid0.pos_error
fault0.fault
@expect vel_int0.acc_out ~ 209.4 1%
@expect max|pid0.pos_error| < 0.0012
@expect fault0.fault == 0
@reject ^ERROR
